# No environment variables are needed. The app is a static export with no
# server, so there is nowhere to keep a secret: anything put in here would be
# compiled into the JavaScript bundle and readable by anyone who opens the site.
#
# Two keys used to live here and no longer do:
#
#   ANTHROPIC_API_KEY — powered an in-app "Ask Claude" lookup route. That route
#     is gone. Ask Claude Code to work out the macros instead; it writes to the
#     same private gist the app syncs with, so the food lands in your log.
#     Removing it also closed a real hole — the route was unauthenticated, so
#     on a public URL anyone could spend your Anthropic credits.
#
#   USDA_API_KEY — powered USDA FoodData Central search. Database search now
#     runs in the browser against Open Food Facts, which needs no key and sends
#     CORS headers that allow it. USDA was dropped rather than shipped with a
#     world-readable key in the bundle.
#
# Sync credentials are not set here either: the GitHub token for gist sync is
# pasted per device and kept in that browser's localStorage.
